      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to compute the sum of the floor values of the square roots of the integers from 1 to 16. Let's break down the steps:\n\n1. Calculate the value of \\(\\lfloor \\sqrt{n} \\rfloor\\) for each integer \\(n\\) from 1 to 16.\n2. Sum these values.\n\nWe can accomplish this by iterating over each integer from 1 to 16, calculating the square root of each integer, then taking the floor value of that square root. Let's do this using Python code.\n```python\n# Define the range of integers\nn_values = range(1, 17)\n\n# Calculate the sum of floor(sqrt(n)) for each n in the range\nimport math\n\nsum_floor_sqrt = sum(math.floor(math.sqrt(n)) for n in n_values)\nprint(sum_floor_sqrt)\n```\n```output\n76\n```\nThe sum of \\(\\lfloor \\sqrt{1} \\rfloor + \\lfloor \\sqrt{2} \\rfloor + \\lfloor \\sqrt{3} \\rfloor + \\cdots + \\lfloor \\sqrt{16} \\rfloor\\) is \\(\\boxed{76}\\).",
